ae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "builds the key as `\"fee_\" + \"rate\"`, so searching the code for `fee_rate` won't find it.\n- Nothing checks for required keys when `settings.json` is loaded (`app/config.py:9-10`), which would have caught this typo straight away.\n\nShould I apply fix 1, fix 2, or both?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nI confirmed three places that read the setting, and nothing reads the misspelled `\"rat\"` key, so renaming it is safe. Applying the fix:\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI fixed the misspelled key in `settings.json`, and all three places that read the setting now get the right value.\n\n**Every place that reads it** (I searched the whole codebase myself, including keys built from pieces like `\"fee_\" + \"rate\"`):\n\n| File:line | How it's read |\n|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, which falls back to 0 if the key is missing |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")` |\n\nAll three get the value from the settings that `app/config.py:9-10` loads from `settings.json`. Nothing reads the old misspelled `\"rat\"` key, so renaming it doesn't break anything. Some other names look similar but aren't this setting: `billing/invoice.py:5` is just a label string, `billing/discount.py:5` is its own local 0.15 value, and `billing/tax.py` and `billing/audit.py` are unrelated.\n\n**The fix:** in `settings.json:2`, I renamed `\"rat\": 0.5` to `\"fee_rate\": 0.5`. That's the only file I changed.\n\n**Results after the fix:**\n- `python3 main.py` now prints `Total: 5.0` (it printed `Total: 0` before)\n- `python3 -m billing.report` now prints `Report fee: 0.5` (it stopped with `fee_rate is missing` before)\n- `python3 -m billing.export.csv_writer` now prints `CSV fee: 0.5`\n\nI didn't change the code in `main.py:12-13` that quietly uses 0 when the key is missing. If the key goes missing again, `main.py` will still print a wrong total with no error. Should I change it to stop with an error the way `report.py` does?", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 163552, "requests_cache_write": 27673, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2746674, "requests_count": 15, "requests_input_uncached": 1563, "requests_output": 4867, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial16", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 60, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T05:09:48.920205+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 3, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 59.001, "t_checker_s": 0.226, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 6430, "tokens_cache_read": 163552, "tokens_cache_write": 27673, "tokens_fresh": 3070, "tokens_input_uncached": 1563, "tokens_main_cache_read": 130012, "tokens_main_cache_write": 13574, "tokens_main_calls": 8, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_output": 3050, "tokens_output": 4867, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 163552, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 27673, "tokens_proxy_calls": 15, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1563, "tokens_proxy_output": 4867, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "